# tools/w/whitepaper_definitions_witness.rish -- the whitepaper row's premise fails, and its own
# falsifier cannot fire.
#
# WHY THIS RUNG. Row 11 of active-designing/date/20260910/20260910-060204_the-bounded-torus-moonshots.md is the
# last unopened row of the twelve, and unlike the other eleven it makes no claim about the world.
# It claims something about the other rows: "One paper binds the three definitions the other eleven
# rows lean on: what a BOUND is when space wraps, what a RADIUS is when privilege is distance, and
# what a TOPOS is when every proof is a cycle." Its assumption is that at least two rows go green
# first and the definitions survive contact; its falsifier is that the first two green witnesses
# give definitions that pull against each other. Nine rows now carry landed readings, so both are
# checkable -- and they are checked by RUNNING the sibling instruments and reading their emitted
# keys rather than by reading the errata that describe them, so the answer moves when an instrument
# moves rather than when somebody remembers to edit a sentence.
#
# ONE DEFINITION OF THREE STANDS. D1, a bound when space wraps, holds: bearing_quorum reads
# cost_half=stands and wrap_worth_one_cut=yes. D2, a radius when privilege is distance, is refuted
# on three independent keys across two instruments -- capability_lattice reads 32 incomparable
# unordered pairs where a line would read 0, and 48 conferrals a radius-only checker would
# over-admit where a line would read 0, while aether_falloff reads a mapped saturation radius of 2
# where a falloff needs at least three distinct radii to grade anything. D3, a topos when every
# proof is a cycle, is left unrun: its instrument is the rostered cyclic_witness, which is
# tier cadence because it RUNS other witnesses to digest their residue.
#
# AND THE UNRUN ONE CANNOT CHANGE THE ANSWER, which the scan proves rather than asserts by
# recomputing the shape reading with D3 forced to stand: finding_robust_to_def3=yes.
#
# THE SHAPE COMES OUT A RING. Each definition states how many independent cycles the space must
# carry. A period needs one; a name and a privilege on separate axes need two, which is the
# proposal page's own sentence. The maximum among the SUPPORTED definitions reads 1, so the
# surviving definitions rest on a circle while the page is titled for a torus. That is two ideas
# wearing one name -- which is row 11's own falsifier, arriving along an axis its sentence never
# named. The second axis is the one thing a torus has that a ring does not, and torus_place already
# read second_axis_buys_spread=no one row over.
#
# THE FALSIFIER CANNOT FIRE AT ALL, which is the sharper half and the reason this is a witness
# rather than a note. Each definition bounds the space FROM BELOW -- D1 needs a cycle to exist, it
# does not need a second one to be absent -- and lower bounds compose by maximum, so no pair of
# standing definitions can be jointly unsatisfiable. The scan enumerates all 27 assignments of the
# three verdicts and counts the conflicting ones under both readings of that hinge: 0 under
# `atleast`, the reading argued above, and 5 under `exact`, in which a one-axis definition would
# refuse a two-axis space. So the falsifier watches for a failure these definitions are structurally
# incapable of having, while the failure they DID have went unwatched.
#
# THAT HINGE IS AN INFERENCE, named as one. Whether a definition's axis count is a floor or an exact
# requirement is a reading of the proposal's prose rather than a measurement, so both answers are
# printed and a reader who disagrees has one place to say so.
#
# WHAT IS GATED, and why all of it. Every figure is either arithmetic over the assignment space or a
# key emitted by a sibling instrument that is itself gated, and the classification thresholds are
# the values a definition HOLDING would produce -- zero incomparable pairs, zero over-admissions,
# three distinct radii. None is a ratchet, because none is a count of this tree's own population
# that ordinary work moves.
#
# WHAT IS PROVEN, on metal, by tools/fixtures/w/whitepaper_definitions_control.sh -- 55 behaviors in
# throwaway pens whose sibling scans are stubs emitting chosen keys, so every branch is reached from
# both sides:
#
#   D2 RESTORED, by planting zero incomparable pairs, zero over-admissions and three radii, reads
#     premise_holds=yes and shape_supported=torus. The refutation is shown from the other side, or
#     it cannot be told from a scan that always refuses.
#   EACH OF D2's THREE KEYS ALONE refutes it, and a fourth pen raising only the saturation radius
#     restores it, so no single key is carrying the verdict by accident.
#   EACH OF D1's TWO KEYS ALONE refutes it, dropping the supported set to zero and the shape to
#     none.
#   A MISSING KEY IS REFUSED rather than defaulted, proven on every one of the six and on all six at
#     once, because an instrument that broke and a definition that stands must never read alike.
#   AN ABSENT SIBLING SCAN is the same refusal, as are an unreadable root and an unknown flag.
#
#   And five mutations, each proven landed by cmp before its reading is believed: a missing key
#   defaulted instead of counted, the incomparable-pairs test dropped, the saturation floor lowered
#   to something every population clears, the shape reported as a torus whatever the survivors need,
#   and the exact-semantics sweep collapsed onto the atleast one so the hinge is hidden.
#
# TWO FAULTS THE PEN FOUND IN THE SCAN, both fixed before this rung was written. The missing-key
# counter was incremented inside a command substitution, so it read zero while four keys were
# absent. And each of the three per-definition lines carried a bare `verdict=` key, so a reader
# taking the first match read a definition's classification as the scan's own answer.
#
# WHAT IT LEAVES TO OTHERS. Whether the paper is worth writing, which is a judgment rather than a
# reading. Whether these are the RIGHT three definitions, which is the proposal's choice. D3's own
# instrument, named above and left to a cadence-tier lap. Any row of the twelve bearing on none of
# the three.
#
# Style: context/GAUGE_STYLE.md
# Paper: active-designing/date/20260915/20260915-212827_the-paper-that-checked-its-own-premise.md
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/w/whitepaper_definitions_witness.rish

say "whitepaper-definitions: Language EN -- a paper's premise is a claim like any other."
say "whitepaper-definitions: Style Gauge, Meter -- every definition names the keys that judge it."
say "whitepaper-definitions: Lens TAME -- refuse a partial read, prove each branch from both sides."

let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/w/whitepaper_definitions_control.sh"]
say control.out
assert control.ok else "whitepaper-definitions: the control must complete -- its own lines are printed above"

assert control.out contains "control_legs_expected=55" else "whitepaper-definitions: the control counts its own legs, so a shrunken pen cannot read as a full one"
assert control.out contains "control_legs=55" else "whitepaper-definitions: a leg added or lost is a leg nobody heard"
assert control.out contains "control_failed=0" else "whitepaper-definitions: every behavior must be satisfied"
assert control.out contains "control_verdict=ok" else "whitepaper-definitions: the control must balance before it is believed"

# Each mutation proven landed before its reading, so a plant that changed no byte cannot pass.
assert control.out contains "leg mutation_default_missing_landed ok" else "whitepaper-definitions: the defaulted-key plant must land before its reading"
assert control.out contains "leg mutation_default_missing_bites ok" else "whitepaper-definitions: a missing key defaulted to zero must change the reading"
assert control.out contains "leg mutation_drop_incomp_landed ok" else "whitepaper-definitions: the dropped-incomparable plant must land"
assert control.out contains "leg mutation_drop_incomp_bites ok" else "whitepaper-definitions: dropping the incomparable-pairs test must change the reading"
assert control.out contains "leg mutation_loosen_satrad_landed ok" else "whitepaper-definitions: the loosened-radius plant must land"
assert control.out contains "leg mutation_loosen_satrad_bites ok" else "whitepaper-definitions: a floor every population clears must change the reading"
assert control.out contains "leg mutation_shape_always_torus_landed ok" else "whitepaper-definitions: the always-torus plant must land"
assert control.out contains "leg mutation_shape_always_torus_bites ok" else "whitepaper-definitions: a shape reported without reading the survivors must change the reading"
assert control.out contains "leg mutation_hide_hinge_landed ok" else "whitepaper-definitions: the collapsed-semantics plant must land"
assert control.out contains "leg mutation_hide_hinge_bites ok" else "whitepaper-definitions: hiding the exact-semantics reading must change the answer"

# A missing key is refused rather than defaulted -- the fault the pen found in the scan itself.
assert control.out contains "leg missing_all_counted ok" else "whitepaper-definitions: six absent keys must count as six"
assert control.out contains "leg missing_all_refused ok" else "whitepaper-definitions: a partial read classifies nothing"
assert control.out contains "leg absent_sibling_refused ok" else "whitepaper-definitions: an absent sibling scan refuses"

# The refutation shown from the other side.
assert control.out contains "leg d2ok_premise ok" else "whitepaper-definitions: privilege back on a line must restore the premise"
assert control.out contains "leg d2ok_shape ok" else "whitepaper-definitions: a standing two-axis definition must read the shape as a torus"

let scan = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/w/whitepaper_definitions_scan.sh"]
say scan.out
assert scan.ok else "whitepaper-definitions: the reading must complete"

assert scan.out contains "keys_absent=0" else "whitepaper-definitions: every bearing instrument must answer before a definition is classified"

# The three definitions, each judged by the keys named in the header.
assert scan.out contains "def1_verdict=supported" else "whitepaper-definitions: the bound-when-space-wraps definition stands on bearing_quorum"
assert scan.out contains "def2_verdict=refuted" else "whitepaper-definitions: privilege is a Boolean lattice and the mapped population saturates at two radii"
assert scan.out contains "def2_axes=2" else "whitepaper-definitions: a name and a privilege on separate axes is the two-axis definition"
assert scan.out contains "definitions_refuted=1" else "whitepaper-definitions: exactly one of the three is refuted by landed readings"

# The shape the survivors need, and the proof that the unrun definition cannot move it.
assert scan.out contains "max_axes_among_supported=1" else "whitepaper-definitions: the surviving definitions need one cycle, not two"
assert scan.out contains "finding_robust_to_def3=yes" else "whitepaper-definitions: the unrun definition must not be able to change the shape"
assert scan.out contains "shape_claimed=torus" else "whitepaper-definitions: the page is titled for a torus"
assert scan.out contains "shape_supported=ring" else "whitepaper-definitions: what the survivors rest on is a circle"
assert scan.out contains "premise_holds=no" else "whitepaper-definitions: the paper's own premise fails"

# The falsifier cannot fire, under the reading this rung argues for -- and could, under the other.
assert scan.out contains "assignments=27" else "whitepaper-definitions: all three verdicts over three definitions is 27 assignments"
assert scan.out contains "conflict_assignments_atleast=0" else "whitepaper-definitions: lower bounds compose by maximum, so no pair conflicts"
assert scan.out contains "conflict_assignments_exact=5" else "whitepaper-definitions: the hinge must stay visible -- exact requirements would conflict in five"
assert scan.out contains "falsifier_satisfiable=no" else "whitepaper-definitions: row 11 watches for a failure its definitions cannot have"
assert scan.out contains "falsifier_blind_to_failure=yes" else "whitepaper-definitions: the premise fails while the falsifier stays quiet"
assert scan.out contains "verdict=blind" else "whitepaper-definitions: the reading's own name for that state"

say "whitepaper-definitions: GREEN -- one definition of three stands, the survivors need a ring, and row 11's falsifier cannot fire in any of 27 assignments."
